From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:37:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Record GPU memory snapshots and rate-limit micromap budget
 logs

Share the VRAM collector with device-local driver totals and heap locality.
Log the snapshot before writing the flushed marker, before the recorder,
Aftermath and Sentry, under the existing single-handler gate. Preserve the
queue reason with JSON escaping and use process-specific marker temporaries,
two short replacement retries and failure cleanup.

Report free VRAM, the previous OMM budget, use and both thresholds when the
budget drops to zero. Bound the heap collector by its snapshot array.
Record the six test sources omitted from the snapshot using the user fork's
staged index, read only. Build them without silent guards. Cover warning
counts and values, scheduling, reason escaping and stale/failed markers.

Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6.1-sol) <noreply@openai.com>
